<title>USA: Nike Inc Q3 shr rises sharply.</title>
<headline>Nike Inc Q3 shr rises sharply.</headline>
<dateline>BEAVERTON, Ore. 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>NIKE, INC	     QUARTER ENDING		  Y-T-D ENDING</p>
<p> QTR FINL STMT	 2/28/97    2/29/96    2/28/97    2/29/96</p>
<p> REVENUES	   $2,423,648 $1,582,039 $6,812,608 $4,638,817</p>
<p>COSTS &amp; EXPENSES</p>
<p>  COST OF SALES    1,435,427    953,316  4,075,174  2,794,824</p>
<p>  SG&amp;A		   577,579    387,534  1,637,569  1,110,292</p>
<p>  INTEREST EXP	  15,793     12,086     38,687     31,864</p>
<p>  OTHER		    7,716     11,429     16,210     29,053</p>
<p>   TOTAL COSTS     2,036,515  1,364,365  5,767,640  3,966,033</p>
<p> PRE TAX		 387,133    217,674  1,044,968    672,784</p>
<p> TAXES		   150,000     83,800    404,900    259,000</p>
<p> NET INCOME	    237,133    133,874    640,068    413,784</p>
<p> INCOME PER SHARE	 0.80	 0.45	 2.16	 1.41</p>
<p> DIVIDEND		   0.10	 0.08	 0.28	 0.21</p>
<p> NUMBER OF SHARES    297,368    294,212    296,915    292,984</p>
<p>NOTE: Nike also reported record worldwide futures orders for athletic footwear and apparel scheduled for delivery between March and July 1997 total $4.30 billion, 34 percent higher than such orders for the same period last year.</p>
<p>Had the U.S. dollar remained constant at year-ago levels, worldwide futures orders would have increased 37 percent.  </p>
<p>(All numbers in table are in thousands except per share data)</p>
</text>
